    "note": "Amended 2018-08-20; Senate (28-9) and Assembly (57-19) final votes were on this text; the first Senate vote (26-8) was on the introduced text. The bill strikes 'to' and 'a bump fire stock or bump fire stock attachment' in the definition and replaces them with 'to, built into, or used in conjunction with,' and the four-item list. The existing ban itself is in other sections, not reprinted."
